  "summary": "Four studies directly apply representation learning with paired positive and negative examples to the domain of battery health, specifically for estimating battery remaining life [V0095, V0093, V0096, V0094]. These works report performance using varied metrics and datasets. Chen et al. (2019) achieved an accuracy of 0.75 on the GridWatch dataset [V0095], while Duarte et al. (2020) reported an MAE of 0.82 on the ProtMap dataset [V0096]. Adebayo et al. (2026) utilized the CellLife dataset to achieve an AUROC of 0.61 [V0093], and Brennan et al. (2018) reported an F1 score of 0.68 on ToxiBench [V0094].",
